  "catalog": [
    {
      // Hand-written to avoid single folder. New products on ows.digitalearth.se must be added here.
      "name": "Vår data",
      "type": "group",
      "members": [
        {
          "name": "DES Sentinel-2 MSI L2A",
          "type": "wms",
          "url": "https://ows.digitalearth.se/wms",
          "layers": "des_s2_msi_l2a",
          "shareKeys": ["//Vår data/DES Sentinel-2 MSI L2A/des_s2_msi_l2a", "//Vår data/des_s2_msi_l2a"],
          "dateFormat": "isoDate",
          "timeFilterPropertyName": "data_available_for_dates",
          "opacity": 1.0,
          "tileWidth": 512,
          "tileHeight": 512,
          "description": "<p><b>Digital Earth Sweden Sentinel-2 Level 2 Analysis Ready Data Collection</b></p>\
            <p>This product represents analysis-ready surface reflectance imagery over Sweden from the European Space Agency's Sentinel-2 mission. The imagery is captured using the Multispectral Instrument (MSI) sensor aboard Sentinel-2A, Sentinel-2B, and Sentinel-2C.</p>\
            <p>The imagery is produced by Digital Earth Sweden (DES) using the Level 2 Processing System of FORCE (<a href='https://force-eo.readthedocs.io/en/latest/'>FORCE documentation</a>). Processing includes radiometric correction of Sentinel-2 Level 1C data and reprojection to the Swedish reference system SWEREF 99 TM.</p>\
            <p>The resulting product consists of ten spectral bands (B02, B03, B04, B05, B06, B07, B08, B08A, B11, B12) provided at their native spatial resolutions of 10 m (B02, B03, B04, B08) and 20 m (B05, B06, B07, B08A, B11, B12). The product also contains quality assurance information (QAI), allowing per-pixel filtering to desired conditions (e.g., cloud-free) for a particular application.</p>\
            <p>As a result, the DES Sentinel-2 MSI collection is a single, cohesive Analysis Ready Data package that allows analysis of surface reflectance data as-is, without the need for additional corrections.</p>"
        }
      ]
    },
