      "type": "group",
      "members": [
        {
          "name": "Lantmäteriet höjdmodell",
          "type": "wms-group",
          "url": "https://maps.lantmateriet.se/hojdmodell/wms/v1.1?service=wms",
          "excludeMembers": [
            "terranglutning",
            "Terrängskuggning",
            "terranglutning_brunton",
            "ursprung_kvalitet",
            "Ursprung och kvalitet"
          ],
          "description": "<p><b><p>Lantmäteriet WMS service</b></p> \
            <p>Lantmäteriet höjdmodell</p>\
            The product is based on height data from the National Land Elevation Model and visualizes the terrain in the form of slope and hillshading. \
            <p>- Terrängskuggning: The layer contains a grayscale image produced by illuminating an elevation model with a simulated lighting source.<br>\
            - Terränglutning, gråton: The layer contains a grayscale image, with each pixel colored according to its calculated gradient value.<br>\
            - Terränglutning, brunton: The layer is designed to visualize areas with potential soil and rock-related stability problems, in brown and purple tones, respectively.</p>",
          "info": [
            {
              "name": "More information",
              "content": "<p><a href='https://www.lantmateriet.se/sv/geodata/vara-produkter/produktlista/markhojdmodell-visning/'>Markhöjdmodell Visning</a></p>\
                  <a href='https://www.lantmateriet.se/globalassets/geodata/geodataprodukter/ny_nationell_hojdmodell_info_blad-131.pdf'>Ny nationell höjdmodell </a>"
            }
          ],
          "itemProperties": {
            "opacity": 1,
            "tileWidth": 512,
            "tileHeight": 512
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Lantmäteriet ortofoto årsvisa",
          "type": "wms-group",
          "url": "https://maps.lantmateriet.se/ortofoto-ar/wms/v1.2?request=GetCapabilities&version=1.1.1&service=WMS",
          "description": "<p><b><p>Lantmäteriet WMS service</b></p> \
            <p>Lantmäteriet ortofoto årsvisa</p>\
            Orthophotos with a resolution of 0.5 m are available within the entire territory of Sweden bounded by the\
            national border and the border of the maritime territory in the sea, with the exception of areas with \
            only open water. In 2000 there was for the first time a complete national coverage of \
            with digital orthophotos, then with 1 m resolution in b/w. Since then, several \
            updates have been made and the whole country is now covered with orthophotos in both color and \
            color and IR with 0.5 m resolution. As of 2019, orthophotos have a resolution of \
            0.4 m/pixel instead of 0.5 m/pixel and can also be provided as 4-channel orthophotos.\
            <p>Orthophotos are radiometrically processed aerial image data, which are geometrically projected onto an orthogonal map projection using an elevation model.\
            In an orthophoto, the scale or distance between points is not affected by terrain variation, unlike an aerial image which has a central projection.</p>",
          "info": [
            {
              "name": "More information",
              "content": "<p><a href='https://www.lantmateriet.se/sv/geodata/vara-produkter/produktlista/ortofoto-nedladdning/'>Lantmäteriet - Ortofoto nedladdning</a></p>\
                  <a href='https://www.lantmateriet.se/globalassets/geodata/geodataprodukter/flyg--och-satellitbilder/pb_ortofoto_nedladdn.pdf'>Lantmäteriet - Produktbeskrivning: Ortofoto Nedladdning</a>"
            }
          ],
