        {
          "name": "Framtida medelvattenstånd",
          "type": "wms-group",
          "url": "https://opendata-view.smhi.se/SMHI_sealevel/wms",
          "description": "<p><b>SMHI WMS service</b></p>\
         <p>Framtida medelvattenstånd</p>\
         <p>Future mean sea level in RK (Rikets Höjdsystem) 2000 and the approximate future location of the shoreline along \
         the Swedish coast are calculated for several different scenarios the years 2050 and 2100.</p>\
         <p>The calculations are based on projections, which the IPCC considers likely, for 3 different emission scenarios:  SSP1-2.6, SSP2-4.5 and SSP5-8.5.\
         Three different levels are given for each scenario and decade. The three levels are the median and the 17th (low) and 83rd (high) percentiles.</p>\
         The Intergovernmental Panel on Climate Change (IPCC) assessment report AR5 2013-2014 uses scenarios called RCPs, \"Representative Concentration Pathways\". The use of the RCPs aims to provide information on climate change at different concentrations of greenhouse gases in the atmosphere.",
          "info": [
            {
              "name": "More information",
              "content": "<p><a href='https://www.smhi.se/data/utforskaren-oppna-data/framtida-medelvattenstand-baserat-pa-data-fran-ipcc-ar6-wg-1-2021'>SMHI - Framtida medelvattenstånd</a></p>\
            <a href='https://opendata-download.smhi.se/framtida_medelvattenstand/baserat-pa-ipcc-ar6-srocc-2019/Metodbeskrivning.pdf'>SMHI - Framtida medelvattenstånd (Rapportera PDF)</a>"
            }
          ],
